    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Consumer Confidence Falls to 90.8 in July Amid Middle East Conflict.",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index, which measures consumer attitudes and buying intentions, decreased to 90.8 in July 2026 from an upwardly revised 92.2 in June. The Present Situation Index softened for the third consecutive month, and the Expectations Index remained below the 80.0 recessionary threshold since February 2025. This decline, influenced by ongoing conflict in the Middle East, indicates growing consumer pessimism and could lead to reduced discretionary spending on non-essential items like specialty food.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "The Conference Board, PR Newswire, Morningstar, investingLive"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-31",
      "description": "UMich Consumer Sentiment Rises to 55.2 in July, a 5-Month High.",
      "details": "The University of Michigan Consumer Sentiment Index, a key measure of consumer attitudes toward the economy, rose to 55.2 in its final July 2026 reading, up from 47.7 in June. This marks a five-month high, primarily driven by easing gas prices. Improved sentiment generally correlates with increased consumer spending, which could positively impact ROAS and CPA for discretionary brands.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "University of Michigan, Trading Economics, Neil's Newsletter"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-03",
      "description": "US Average Gas Price $4.10/Gallon, Down from May Peak but Up YoY.",
      "details": "The national average price for a gallon of regular gasoline was $4.10 on August 3, 2026. While this was down 8.5% from a recent peak of $4.48 in May, it remained 30.0% higher than a year prior. High gas prices reduce consumers' disposable income, leading to suppressed spending on non-essential goods like specialty food, negatively impacting ROAS and increasing CPA.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "LendingTree, AAA"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-07",
      "description": "US Unemployment Rate Dips to 4.1% in July, Payrolls Fall.",
      "details": "The US unemployment rate, a key indicator of labor market health, decreased to 4.1% in July 2026 from 4.2% in June. This was accompanied by a decline of 23,000 in nonfarm payroll employment. While a lower unemployment rate typically signals a strong economy, the fall in payrolls and a shrinking labor force suggest a more complex picture. This could lead to mixed consumer sentiment, potentially suppressing discretionary spending for some segments.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "Bureau of Labor Statistics, Trading Economics, Hunt Scanlon Media, Kiplinger"
    },
    {
